# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
# Anchored: unanchored, this also matched vendor/source-patches/build-make/ and build-soong/,
# which stayed tracked here only because they predate the rule — and a fresh repository built from
# this tree silently left them out, failing every test that checks registered patches exist.
/build*/
dist/

# tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
# androguard writes this into the CWD on every run, so any APK inspection from the repo root
# leaves one behind (bd remora-9lj's Reddit RE work is where they come from).
androguard.log

# built native artifacts — resolution 0a: build from source, never commit blobs
/vendor/native/fwd
/vendor/native/remora-frame-encoder
/vendor/native/remora-frame-decoder
# the mirror agent's dex, same rule: agent/build.sh compiles agent/src against the lineage tree's
# framework.jar. agent/out/ is scratch; vendor/agent/agent.dex is the deployable copy the engine
# mounts (bd remora-28ix.3).
/agent/out/
/vendor/agent/agent.dex
/vendor/native/uinput-kbd

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/
/build/
# a second CMake tree configured with REMORA_INSTALLED_VENDOR=OFF, so `remora build --source`
# stages the REPO vendor rather than /usr/share/remora/vendor. The default build/ here is
# configured ON, which silently staged a stale do-build.sh through two builds (bd remora-4ei.30).
/build-dev/
# a third tree with the same OFF config as build-dev. 476 files / 27 MB of build output were
# showing up as untracked noise — 476 of the 482 entries in `git status` — which is enough to bury
# the handful of real untracked source files under it.
/build-repovendor/
# a fourth, same OFF config again (host-encoder work). Same 456-file / 23 MB noise problem as the
# one above — which is exactly how it hid: `git status` showed it as a single untracked DIRECTORY,
# so the size never announced itself.
/build-hostenc/

# Deliberately-removed vendored files that keep reappearing untracked. This tree lives under
# ~/.sync (Syncthing), which restores files git has deleted, so without these entries every
# `git status` carries the same stale noise and can bury a real untracked source file.
# Each was removed on purpose — re-adding any of them is a decision, not a cleanup:
#   play_cert/         superseded by the play_spoof build feature
#   vm-rez-install.sh  superseded by the same feature; nothing references it
# uinput-kbd.c came BACK on purpose (bd remora-gf7): persist-kbd.py, the thing that superseded
# it, was itself deleted with the vm backend, and a container has no other way to show Android a
# physical keyboard. It is a committed source with a build rule again; only the built binary is
# ignored, up in the "built native artifacts" block with fwd.
/vendor/source-build/features/play_cert/
/vendor/guest-scripts/vm-rez-install.sh

# Mesa cross-build output staged for the mesa_source feature (bd remora-ykhz / bd remora-bm7.4).
# Build OUTPUT, not vendored prebuilts: ~19 MB per driver, produced by
# vendor/host-prereqs/mesa-android/build-mesa.sh, and stage-features.sh already REFUSES to build
# the feature when this directory is absent — so its absence fails loudly rather than shipping a
# stale driver.
vendor/source-build/features/mesa_source/lib64/

# Third-party binary payloads — never committed here (vendor/PAYLOADS.md).
# vendor/fetch-payloads.sh stages them; a build refuses if an enabled feature's payload is absent.
vendor/**/*.apk
vendor/**/*.so
vendor/**/*.jar
vendor/**/*.dex
vendor/**/*.zip
vendor/**/*.img
vendor/**/*.bin
# ...and the third-party text that travels with them (see EXCLUDE_TEXT in make-public-tree.sh).
vendor/source-build/features/widevine/vendor/
vendor/source-build/features/ndk_translation/etc/
vendor/source-build/features/ndk_translation/guest/
vendor/source-build/features/ndk_translation/lib64/
vendor/source-build/features/gapps/product/
vendor/source-build/features/zygisk_pif/shamiko/*
!vendor/source-build/features/zygisk_pif/shamiko/REMORA.md
